course: dictionary
lesson: 9575
title: Strategic: planned to win
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Strategic means carefully planned to reach a goal. A strategic move is not a lucky guess: someone thought ahead about what would happen next. «She made a strategic move in chess, giving up a pawn to trap the king.» The clue is the planning: she gave something up on purpose so she could win later.
explain: The second meaning is about places and plans that matter for winning. «The castle stood at a strategic point by the river.» A castle there could watch the river and stop enemies crossing, so the place is important for winning. A strategic position is a spot that helps you win.
explain: Strategic is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a strategic plan, a strategic position, strategic thinking. «Strategic withdrawal» is the official way to say an army retreated on purpose, following a plan. Look for clue words such as plan, goal, win or important, and swap in carefully planned to check.
fact: Strategic means carefully planned to reach a goal.
fact: Strategic also means important for winning a war, game or plan.
fact: «Strategic withdrawal» is the official way to say an army retreated on purpose.
fact: Strategic thinking means planning ahead and thinking about what your opponent will do next.
fact: Strategic is an adjective: more strategic, most strategic.
exercise: «The coach made a strategic plan before the match.» What does strategic mean here? | *Carefully planned to reach a goal | Very loud | Old and broken | Lucky and unplanned
exercise: «The castle stood at a strategic point by the river.» Why would a castle be built at a strategic point? | Because it was the cheapest place to buy stone | *Because it was important for watching the river and winning control of it | Because it was the tallest hill around
exercise: Which phrase means a planned retreat? | *Strategic withdrawal | Robust discussion | Loud cheer | Sudden sneeze
test: Ella says a strategic move in chess is just a lucky guess. Is she right? | Yes, because chess is only for luck | Yes, a strategic move is a lucky guess | *No, a strategic move is planned ahead to reach a goal
test: In the phrase «strategic thinking», what kind of word is strategic? | A full stop | *An adjective | A verb | A noun
exam: Which sentence uses strategic correctly? | The children ate a strategic sandwich for lunch | *The team made a strategic plan to win the game | The dog was very strategic and barked at the cat | The rain was strategic and fell on the hill
